#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""slurmtop - a one-screen dashboard for small GPU clusters.

Shows CPU / RAM / per-GPU utilisation for every node plus the Slurm queue,
with colour gradient bars and sparkline history. Nodes are discovered from
Slurm automatically; remote nodes are read over SSH.

    slurmtop                 # refresh every 2s
    slurmtop -n 5            # refresh every 5s
    slurmtop --once          # print once (handy for pasting into chat)
    slurmtop --nodes a,b,c   # explicit node list instead of Slurm discovery
    slurmtop --proc          # also list processes on each GPU
    slurmtop --stack         # force vertical layout
    slurmtop --no-color      # plain text
    slurmtop --lang zh       # 繁體中文介面

Requires only Python 3.8+, nvidia-smi on the nodes, and passwordless SSH to
any remote node. Slurm is optional - without it, pass --nodes.

credited by team-03/Hawks - HiPAC 2026, NCHC
https://github.com/Sean-Hawks/slurmtop
"""

